-- title:
--   Dual of localised cohomology as a summand of 𝒪⊗ TₚJ_H
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, characteristic zero, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\mathcal O$ be a $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra. Let $S\subseteq\mathbb N$, let $N,r\ge 1$, let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to the residue field of $\mathcal O$, let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be primes, let $\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_t$ lie in the residue field, put $L=\mathtt{level}\,N\,r\,q_\bullet=N(\prod_i q_i)r$, and let $H\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$. Assume `OpComm`, that the operators $\mathtt{op}$ indexed by the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$) and $U_i$ ($i\in\mathrm{Fin}\,t$) commute pairwise on the carrier module, and `DiaComm`, that each diamond operator $\langle u\rangle$, $u\in(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$, commutes with all of them. Assume further the non-Eisenstein hypothesis: there is a prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and $\ell\equiv 1 \pmod L$ such that $\theta(T_\ell)\neq \ell+1$ in the residue field. Write $\mathrm{Ta}=\mathcal O\otimes_{\mathbb Z_p}T_p(J_H(L))$, where $J_H(L)$ is the degree-zero divisor class group of the function field of $X_H(L)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $T_p$ is the group of sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$. Then there exists an $\mathcal O$-linear endomorphism $E$ of $\mathrm{Ta}$ with $E\circ E=E$ which commutes with the $\mathcal O$-base change of each operator $\mathtt{tateGenOpH}$ attached to the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$), $U_{q_i}$ and $\langle d\rangle$ ($d\in(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$), and with the base change of $\mathtt{JH.tateGaloisRep}\,\sigma$ for every $\sigma\in\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$; moreover there is an injective $\mathcal O$-linear map $\Theta$ from the $\mathcal O$-dual of `ML`, the localisation of the carrier module at the complement of the prime ideal $\mathfrak m_\theta$ (the kernel of the homomorphism of the free polynomial algebra on the generators determined by $\theta$ and $\alpha$), into $\mathrm{Ta}$, whose range equals the range of $E$, and which carries precomposition of a functional with the action on `ML` of the variables $X_{T_\ell}$ and $X_{U_i}$, and with $\mathtt{diaML}\,u$, to the base-changed operators $\mathtt{tateGenOpH}$ for $T_\ell$, $U_{q_i}$ and $\langle u\rangle$ respectively.
--
--   This is the integral, localised comparison between the cohomology of $\Gamma_H(L)$ and the Tate module of the Jacobian of $X_H(L)$: the $\mathcal O$-dual of the cohomology localised at a non-Eisenstein maximal ideal is realised, Hecke-equivariantly and compatibly with the Galois action, as the image of an idempotent on $\mathcal O\otimes_{\mathbb Z_p}T_pJ_H(L)$, the cohomological operators corresponding to the covariant Hecke operators on the Jacobian. It feeds the construction of the faithful Galois- and Hecke-stable lattice with Frobenius and torsion data used at Taylor–Wiles auxiliary levels.
